-- title:
--   Newform behind a weight-two Hecke point with uₚ ∣ p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N\ge 1$, and $S$ a finite set of naturals containing every prime divisor of $N$; let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a commutative integral domain of characteristic zero. Here [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$ with $q\notin S$. Given a ring homomorphism $\chi$ from this algebra to $\mathcal{O}'$, a prime $p\mid N$, and $u_p\in\mathcal{O}'$, assume $\chi$ extends along the inclusion of [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) into [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (S \ {p})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the larger algebra, obtained by adjoining $U_p$) to a homomorphism $\chi'$ with $\chi'(U_p)=u_p$, and that $u_p\mid p$ in $\mathcal{O}'$. Then there are $M_g\ne 0$ dividing $N$ and $g\in S_2(\Gamma_0(M_g))$ satisfying `IsNewform`, i.e. $g$ is a normalized eigenform (its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity at coprime indices, and the prime-power recursions $a_{q^{r+2}}=a_qa_{q^{r+1}}-q\,a_{q^r}$ for $q\nmid M_g$ and $a_{q^{r+2}}=a_qa_{q^{r+1}}$ for $q\mid M_g$) and no proper divisor of $M_g$ carries a normalized eigenform with the same $a_\ell$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M_g$; together with a ring homomorphism $\chi_g$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra Mg 2 (S \ {p})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $\mathbb{C}$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for primes $\ell\nmid M_g$, $\ell\notin S\setminus\{p\}$, and $\chi_g(U_p)=a_p(g)$ if $p\mid M_g$, and a ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal{O}'$ such that $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))=\chi(T_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, and such that either $p\nmid M_g$ and $u_p^2-\iota(\chi_g(T_p))u_p+p=0$ in $\mathcal{O}'$, or $p\mid M_g$, $p^2\nmid M_g$ and $\iota(\chi_g(U_p))=u_p$.
--
--   This is the $p$-old/$p$-new dichotomy for a weight-two Hecke eigensystem whose $U_p$-value divides $p$: either the eigensystem comes from a newform of level prime to $p$ and $u_p$ is a root of that newform's Hecke polynomial $X^2-a_p(g)X+p$, or it comes from a newform of level exactly divisible by $p$ with $a_p(g)$ matching $u_p$. It is the companion, in the non-unit case, of the corresponding statement for a unit $U_p$-value, and is used in the construction of Galois representations attached to Hecke points and in the ordinarity/flatness analysis at $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_isNewform_of_point_of_up_dvd.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_Newforms

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.exists_isNewform_of_point_of_up_dvd
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (S : Finset ℕ)
    (hNS : ∀ q : ℕ, q.Prime → q ∣ N → q ∈ S)
    (𝒪' : Type) [CommRing 𝒪'] [IsDomain 𝒪'] [CharZero 𝒪']
    (χ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (↑S : Set ℕ) →+* 𝒪')
    (hpN : p ∣ N) (up : 𝒪')
    (hup : ∃ χ' : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ((↑S : Set ℕ) \ {p}) →+* 𝒪',
      (∀ t : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (↑S : Set ℕ),
        χ' (Subalgebra.inclusion (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra_mono Set.diff_subset) t) = χ t) ∧
      χ' (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.U (Fact.out : p.Prime) hpN (by simp)) = up)
    (hdvd : up ∣ (p : 𝒪')) :
    ∃ (Mg : ℕ) (_ : NeZero Mg) (hMgN : Mg ∣ N)
      (g : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 Mg) 2) (_ : g.IsNewform)
      (chig : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra Mg 2 ((↑S : Set ℕ) \ {p}) →+* ℂ)
      (_ : ∀ (ℓ : ℕ) (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) (hℓMg : ¬ ℓ ∣ Mg) (hℓS : ℓ ∉ ((↑S : Set ℕ) \ {p})),
        chig (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T hℓ hℓMg hℓS) = ModularFormClass.qCoeff g ℓ)
      (_ : ∀ (hpMg : p ∣ Mg),
        chig (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.U (Fact.out : p.Prime) hpMg (by simp)) =
          ModularFormClass.qCoeff g p)
      (iota : chig.range →+* 𝒪'),
      (∀ (ℓ : ℕ) (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) (hℓN : ¬ ℓ ∣ N) (hℓS : ℓ ∉ (↑S : Set ℕ)),
        iota (chig.rangeRestrict (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T hℓ
          (fun h => hℓN (h.trans hMgN)) (fun h => hℓS (Set.mem_of_mem_diff h)))) =
          χ (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T hℓ hℓN hℓS)) ∧
      ((∃ hpMg : ¬ p ∣ Mg,
          up * up - iota (chig.rangeRestrict
            (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T (Fact.out : p.Prime) hpMg (by simp))) * up + (p : 𝒪') = 0) ∨
       (∃ hpMg : p ∣ Mg, ¬ p ^ 2 ∣ Mg ∧
          iota (chig.rangeRestrict
            (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.U (Fact.out : p.Prime) hpMg (by simp))) = up)) := by sorry
